1
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:26,000
The animated House Musical.

2
00:08:40,000 --> 00:08:46,000
Interstella 5555: The 5tory of the 5ecret 5tar 5ystem is a animation,
science fiction, music film directed by Kazuhisa Takenouchi.

3
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:06,000
Four talented alien musicians are kidnapped by a record
producer who disguises them as humans.

4
00:17:20,000 --> 00:17:26,000
Shep, a space pilot in love with bass player Stella, follows them to Earth.

5
00:21:40,000 --> 00:21:46,000
Reprogrammed to forget their real identities and renamed The Crescendolls, the
group quickly becomes a huge success playing soulless corporate pop.

6
00:26:00,000 --> 00:26:06,000
At a concert, Shep manages to free all the musicians except Stella, and the band
sets out to rediscover who they really are — and to rescue Stella.

7
00:30:20,000 --> 00:30:26,000
Octave (singing voice), played by Romanthony.

8
00:34:40,000 --> 00:34:46,000
Shep (singing voice), played by Thomas Bangalter.

9
00:39:00,000 --> 00:39:06,000
Interstella 5555: The 5tory of the 5ecret 5tar 5ystem (インターステラ5555, Intāsutera Fō
Faibu; "Four Five") is a 2003 anime musical science fiction film.

10
00:43:20,000 --> 00:43:26,000
The film tells the story of the abduction and rescue of an extraterrestrial pop band and
serves as a visual companion to Discovery, Daft Punk's second studio album.

11
00:47:40,000 --> 00:47:46,000
The film was produced by Toei Animation, directed by Kazuhisa
Takenouchi and supervised by Leiji Matsumoto.

12
00:52:00,000 --> 00:52:06,000
The film has no dialogue, but instead consists of the
entirety of Discovery with minimal sound effects.

13
00:56:20,000 --> 00:56:26,000
The film explores themes of rescue, spaceman,
musical, record producer, music video.

14
01:00:40,000 --> 01:00:46,000
The tone is thought_provoking.
